// Barnacle Bay — Shared Beats
//
// Reusable nodes called via <<detour>> from harbour.bub.
// Demonstrates the multi-file split: the map seller lives here so this beat
// could be reused from any number of scenes without duplicating the script.
//
// This file is compiled together with harbour.bub:
//   cargo run -p bubbles-tui -- examples/harbour/harbour.bub examples/harbour/services.bub Harbour
//
// Features demonstrated in this file:
//   - <<detour>> target node (called from harbour.bub, returns to caller)
//   - Multi-node file (MapSeller node)
//   - <<if>> / <<elseif>> / <<else>> conditional chain

title: MapSeller
---
MapSeller: Psst. Charts, maps, treasure coordinates — all freshly forged.

<<if $gold >= 15>>
    MapSeller: For fifteen doubloons I'll sell ye a map to the Sunken Galleon.
    MapSeller: Rumour has it the hold's still full of cursed gold.
    -> Buy the map for fifteen doubloons.
        <<set $gold = $gold - 15>>
        <<give_map "sunken_galleon">>
        MapSeller: Pleasure doing business. Don't say I never warned ye about the curse.
    -> Decline.
        MapSeller: Suit yerself. Offer won't stand forever.
<<elseif $gold >= 5>>
    MapSeller: Can't afford the good stuff, but I've a rough sketch for five doubloons.
    MapSeller: Might be accurate. Might not.
    -> Buy the sketch for five doubloons.
        <<set $gold = $gold - 5>>
        <<give_map "rough_sketch">>
        MapSeller: There ye go. Best of luck interpreting me handwriting.
    -> Decline.
        MapSeller: No shame in it. Come back when yer pockets are heavier.
<<else>>
    MapSeller: Ha! Not a doubloon to yer name, have ye?
    MapSeller: Come back when ye've got coin, friend.
<<endif>>

<<return>>
===
